 "notes": "TOKENIZER: comments are // to end of line (no block comments); compiler annotations are comments starting with //@ ; the first line MUST be exactly //@version=6 (any other //@version=N is an error). Strings: double or single quotes, backslash escapes, no multi-line strings. Identifiers: [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]* joined by '.', match the longest dotted name first (strategy.commission.percent before strategy.commission). 'namespaces' maps root -> member suffix (so strategy -> commission.percent). LINT RULES: (1) every dotted identifier whose root is a key in 'namespaces' MUST have its suffix in that list; a root that is not a namespace key is a user variable (UDT field / method call), then accept if the last segment is in 'methods' or the root was declared in-file. (2) undotted identifiers MUST be in keywords|types|variables|functions, or declared in-file (assignment 'x =', typed 'float x =', 'var'/'varip', function 'f(...) =>', 'for x =', 'for x in', tuple '[a, b] =', 'method'/'type'/'enum' names, import aliases). (3) any name in 'deprecated' is an error (v4/v5 leftover) — but only for identifiers NOT declared in-file (a user variable named e.g. 'atr' or 'rsi' is legal; the deprecated hit is the bare v4 function call form 'rsi(' / 'sma(' etc.). (4) named argument in 'deprecated_params' is an error only inside strategy.*() / plot*() / input*() calls ('type' is also a keyword, so only flag it as a named argument 'type =' inside input()). (5) 'warn' items are allowed but must be reported as warnings (repaint / fill-model changers), never silently. Built-in numeric args to strategy() must be literals (const): flag input.* or variables passed to strategy(). Overload arity is NOT encoded here; the reference 'syntax' strings live in scratchpad pine/v6_ref_parsed.json if a later lint wants them."
